                <pb facs="0345" n="295" xml:id="pg295"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. E. Alexander to Mr. Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * The draft of a trade-mark convention
                    has been submitted to the minister for foreign affairs, who is now considering
                    the matter. In May I had several conferences with him on this subject. It is
                    probable that the convention can be concluded at once.</p>
                <p>I am translating the laws of Greece relating to trademarks, and will send you the
                    translation as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Alexander.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
